+++ b/docs-xml/manpages/vfs_aio_fork.8.xml
@@ -43,15 +43,32 @@
 	<para>To work around all these limitations, the aio_fork module
 	was written. It uses forked helper processes instead of the
 	internal Posix AIO interface to create asynchronousity for
-	read and write calls. It has no parameters, it will create
-	helper processes when async requests come in as needed. Idle
-	helper processes will be removed every 30 seconds.
+	read and write calls. It creates helper processes when async
+	requests come in as needed. This Time Capsule build checks for idle
+	helper processes every three hours.
 	</para>
 
 	<para>This module is stackable.</para>
 
 </refsect1>
 
+<refsect1>
+	<title>OPTIONS</title>
+
+	<variablelist>
+		<varlistentry>
+			<term>aio_fork:max_children = INTEGER</term>
+			<listitem>
+				<para>Limit the number of helper processes for this
+				share connection. When all helpers are busy, the module
+				queues at most 16 requests and then performs
+				additional requests synchronously. The default value of
+				zero leaves the number of helpers unlimited.</para>
+			</listitem>
+		</varlistentry>
+	</variablelist>
+</refsect1>
+
 
